{"name":"Caicos Turquoise","hex":"#26b7b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turquoise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sky-blue, greenish-blue, or greenish-gray semi-precious gemstone.","A pale greenish-blue colour, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of turquoise (the gemstone).","Having a pale greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turquoise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turks and Caicos Islands","blocks":[{"text":"Turks and Caicos Islands is a British Overseas Territory consisting of the larger Caicos Islands and smaller Turks Islands, two groups of tropical islands in the Lucayan Archipelago of the Atlantic Ocean and northern West Indies. They are known primarily for tourism and as an offshore financial centre. The resident population in 2023 was estimated by The World Factbook at 59,367, making it the third-largest of the British overseas territories by population. However, according to a Department of Statistics estimate in 2022, the population was 47,720."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_the_Turks_and_Caicos_Islands.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Turks_and_Caicos_Islands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turks_and_Caicos_Islands","wikidata":"Q18221"},{"title":"Turquoise","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is an opaque, blue-to-green mineral that is a hydrous phosphate of copper and aluminium, with the chemical formula CuAl6(PO4)4(OH)8·4H2O. It is rare and valuable in finer grades and has been prized as a gemstone for millennia due to its hue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Turquoise-40031.jpg/330px-Turquoise-40031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise","wikidata":"Q165254"},{"title":"Turquoise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is a cyan color, based on the mineral of the same name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise_(color)","wikidata":"Q5960345"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Turks_and_Caicos_Islands_raking_salt_stamp_1938.jpg/500px-Turks_and_Caicos_Islands_raking_salt_stamp_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Turks_and_Caicos_Islands_raking_salt_stamp_1938.jpg/500px-Turks_and_Caicos_Islands_raking_salt_stamp_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Raking salt on a 1938 postage stamp of the islands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurks_and_Caicos_Islands_raking_salt_stamp_1938.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg/500px-Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg/1280px-Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg/500px-Historic_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 1852 lighthouse on Grand Turk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistoric_Lighthouse_Park_on_Grand_Turk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Sharlene-cartwright-robinson.png/330px-Sharlene-cartwright-robinson.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Sharlene-cartwright-robinson.png/330px-Sharlene-cartwright-robinson.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut